{%- comment -%}
The Available Cuts index (live /available-cuts), driven by Shopify data
rather than the crawl.

The live page is a frozen snapshot: it lists all 54 cuts with no sold-out
state at all, so a shopper browsing the page named "Available cuts" sees
cuts that cannot be bought — and the live /all-japanese-wagyu grid marks 41
of those same 54 as sold out. Here the page means what it says: each group
lists only what is actually purchasable right now (in stock and priced), so
every card leads to a product that can be added to the cart.

Same primal grouping and copy as /collections/all.
{%- endcomment -%}
